# AN AFTERNOON IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD — provisional complete short-story flow.
# Original external game, not part of the narrative-engine test fixtures.
# Three outcomes reflect authored choices and optional conversations.

@scene intro
set met_elena = false
set met_mateo = false
set met_rosa = false
set heard_elena = false
set mateo_wants_help = false
set heard_rosa = false
set saw_ledger = false
set respected_privacy = false
set read_display = false
set stroked_cat = false
set remembered_door = false
set board_postponed = false
set welcome = "returning"
background street
music golden_hour
"The sun sinks slowly over the neighborhood rooftops. The streets seem smaller than they did before you left."
"The corner shop's shutter is raised. Behind the counter, you recognize a face."
"You didn't come back to fix anyone's life. You repeat that to yourself as you walk toward the noticeboard."
"The shop is open. You can go in and speak to Mateo, return to the street, or leave your answer on the board."
explore street at home

@scene elena_chat
music golden_hour
surface bubble
if met_elena == true
elena: "You're back. Looks like these old streets still have something to say."
"Elena steps aside to let a bicycle pass. This time she doesn't need to ask who you are."
else
set met_elena = true
elena: "Well, look at you. Do you still remember how to find this street?"
"Elena adjusts her backpack and glances toward the jacaranda tree."
end
* "I left, but I never forgot the way." -> elena_welcome
* "I don't know if I still belong here." -> elena_uncertain
* "What happened to Mateo's shop?" -> elena_news

@scene elena_welcome
set heard_elena = true
elena: "Then you must remember you can't step outside without running into someone."
elena: "Everyone's talking about the shop today. There's a new notice on the board."
"Her eyes rest for a moment on the papers pinned to the wall."
explore return

@scene elena_uncertain
set heard_elena = true
elena: "Some days I don't either. You don't have to agree with a street to love it."
elena: "The shop might close. I wanted you to hear it from someone, not from a piece of paper."
"She gives you room to answer; you don't. She doesn't seem to need you to."
explore return

@scene elena_news
set heard_elena = true
elena: "They raised his rent, and now they're talking about selling the place. You know how that starts."
elena: "But Mateo doesn't want anyone turning him into a cause without asking him first."
"Elena brushes a strand of hair from her face. She doesn't look angry. She looks tired."
explore return

@scene rosa_chat
music golden_hour
surface bubble
if met_rosa == true
rosa: "Seems nobody can even agree on what time to hold the meeting."
"Rosa folds a paper bag between her hands. She recognizes you and continues without starting from the beginning."
else
set met_rosa = true
rosa: "Are you here about the notice too? I thought it was the only gossip in town this week."
"Rosa smooths her apron and studies the posters as though looking for a familiar signature."
rosa: "Everyone has their own version. The street changes even when nobody moves."
end
* "What are the customers saying?" -> rosa_people
* "What do you think should be done?" -> rosa_opinion
* "I'm still catching up." -> rosa_later

@scene rosa_people
set heard_rosa = true
rosa: "One woman wants a bigger shop. A boy says Mateo lets him buy on credit when he's short of money."
rosa: "All of that can be true at once. The hard part is listening without choosing a side first."
explore return

@scene rosa_opinion
set heard_rosa = true
rosa: "I don't know. I've been shopping here in the evenings for years. That isn't a public policy."
rosa: "If we're getting people together, Mateo should at least be there to speak for himself."
explore return

@scene rosa_later
rosa: "Well, you've still got time. The sun hasn't set yet."
explore return

@scene mateo_chat
music shop_hush
surface bubble
if met_mateo == true
mateo: "You're still here. At least you can listen to me more than once before deciding for me."
"Mateo moves a box aside to serve someone who just walked in, then turns back to you."
else
sound shop_bell
"The little bell above the door rings. Someone has come in to buy bread for dinner."
set met_mateo = true
mateo: "You showed up just when everyone has an opinion about my business. Lucky me."
end
if saw_ledger == true
"He glances toward the notebook where he recorded last month's stock."
mateo: "If you came for the numbers, they aren't the whole story."
end
if respected_privacy == true
mateo: "Thanks for not digging through my accounts. Not everyone understands that."
end
"Behind Mateo, afternoon sunlight catches in the glass bottles."
mateo: "Elena wants to call a meeting. To be honest, I just want one afternoon without outstanding bills."
* "We could listen to what you need." -> mateo_help
* "Closing can be your decision too." -> mateo_choice
* "Does it bother you that people want to help?" -> mateo_anger

@scene mateo_help
set mateo_wants_help = true
mateo: "Maybe. If somebody offers to listen before putting up a pretty poster, maybe."
"He straightens a packet of rice on the shelf and rests his hand there."
mateo: "I'd like to make a decision without feeling that I owe everyone a happy ending."
explore return

@scene mateo_choice
set mateo_wants_help = false
mateo: "Thank you. So far everyone talks about the shop. Nobody asks about me."
"The refrigerator hum fills a silence that doesn't feel uncomfortable."
mateo: "I'm not saying no to the meeting. I just want it to remain my decision."
explore return

@scene mateo_anger
set mateo_wants_help = false
mateo: "No. What bothers me is everyone assuming that staying is the only way to love this place."
mateo: "My father opened this shop with a loan. I grew up here. That doesn't mean I have to die here."
"Outside, a bicycle bell rings."
explore return

@scene shop_cat
music shop_hush
surface bubble
if stroked_cat == true
"This time the cat opens both eyes when it hears your footsteps. It doesn't get up, but it lets you approach without pretending you're still a stranger."
else
"A white cat with brown patches sleeps beside the old newspapers. It seems to know the business better than anyone."
"It opens one eye as you approach, then closes it again with all the patience in the world."
end
* "Gently pet its head." -> shop_cat_pet
* "Let it sleep and keep exploring." -> shop_cat_sleep

@scene shop_cat_pet
set stroked_cat = true
"The cat allows one stroke, then settles its head against your fingers as if it has made an important decision."
"You stay there for a moment. Some afternoons don't demand an immediate answer."
explore return

@scene shop_cat_sleep
"You don't interrupt its nap. Under the lamplight, the shop seems to be breathing very slowly."
explore return

@scene shop_display
music shop_hush
surface bubble
if read_display == true
"The price tags are still in place. The box reminds you of the candy Mateo once gave you; now you recognize his handwriting on the prices."
else
"The shelves are full of things people buy without thinking: candles, soap, cans of tuna."
"On the lowest shelf sits a little box of old price labels, handwritten."
end
* "Remember shopping here long ago." -> shop_display_remember
* "Get back to what you were doing." -> shop_display_leave

@scene shop_display_remember
set read_display = true
"When you were younger, Mateo gave you a piece of candy because you'd forgotten to bring change."
"You remember the embarrassment better than the taste of the candy."
explore return

@scene shop_display_leave
"The refrigerator hums. Not every object has to become a memory."
explore return

@scene shop_ledger
music shop_hush
surface panel
"The account book rests beside the register. Someone has left a pencil between its last pages."
"You could look at the debts, but Mateo hasn't given you permission."
* "Leave it closed and ask Mateo directly." -> shop_ledger_respect
* "Take a look at the accounts." -> shop_ledger_read
* "Leave it as it is." -> shop_ledger_leave

@scene shop_ledger_respect
if saw_ledger == true
"This time you leave it closed. Having seen those accounts before didn't give you permission."
else
set respected_privacy = true
"You don't open the notebook. If you want to know what Mateo needs, you'll have to ask him."
end
explore return

@scene shop_ledger_read
set saw_ledger = true
set respected_privacy = false
sound paper_rustle
"You can't make sense of every figure. You can only see that some neighbors' accounts have been open for months."
"The notebook doesn't tell you who gets to make Mateo's decisions, either."
explore return

@scene shop_ledger_leave
"There's nothing urgent in those pages for someone who has only just returned to solve."
explore return

@scene threshold_memory
music golden_hour
surface panel
if remembered_door == true
"The scratches are still there, even though you've remembered who opened the door for you one afternoon. You don't have to knock again to know it happened."
else
"The wooden door still bears the scratches from the year you learned to ride a bicycle. Someone has painted around them, never over them."
"Through a window you hear dishes and a radio. You don't recognize the song, but you know the sound of someone making dinner."
end
* "Remember an afternoon before you left." -> threshold_remember
* "Keep walking. Not everything needs to become a memory." -> threshold_walk

@scene threshold_remember
set remembered_door = true
"You see yourself as a child, standing here with a bag of bread and the absurd fear of knocking on the wrong door."
"The neighborhood wasn't yours then. Still, someone opened the door and let you in."
explore return

@scene threshold_walk
"You keep your hand away from the doorknob. That house has its own afternoon, and you don't need to enter it."
explore return

@scene board_read
music golden_hour
surface panel
if board_postponed == true
"You return to the noticeboard. The pencil is still tied to the same string, but now you know you didn't have to answer on your first visit."
"The notice is still there. You've returned, but that doesn't mean you have to decide for Mateo."
else
"THE SQUARE NOTICEBOARD. A room for rent, guitar lessons, a missing bicycle, and three notices in the same handwriting."
"A new sheet proposes a neighborhood meeting before anyone decides the shop's future. There's space below for a reply."
end
if met_elena == true
"You remember Elena, who spoke of the street as though it needed someone to listen to it too."
end
if met_rosa == true
"Rosa reminded you that neighbors' stories never fit completely on a single notice."
end
if met_mateo == true
"Mateo would rather not be made to represent the entire neighborhood's nostalgia."
end
if saw_ledger == true
"You know the figures you saw in the shop don't explain who should make the decision."
end
if respected_privacy == true
"You chose not to read the accounts without permission. The notice should respect that same boundary."
end
"The pencil tied to the board is worn down, but it still writes."
* "Invite everyone to listen, starting with Mateo." -> ending_listen
* "Offer a concrete plan to help keep the shop open." -> ending_open
* "Put down the pencil and let others take the initiative." -> ending_quiet
* "I need to talk to someone before I answer." -> board_return

@scene board_return
set board_postponed = true
"You set the pencil down against its string. You don't have to decide now, and the board will still be here when you return."
"You hear a bell from the shop and footsteps coming down the stairs."
explore return

@scene ending_listen
mode visual_novel
background street_evening
surface panel
if board_postponed == true
"This time you don't write immediately. Setting the pencil down for a while reminded you that a conversation deserves more than a quick reply."
end
if remembered_door == true
"You think of the old doorway where someone made room for you without demanding an explanation. Perhaps listening is a similar way of opening a door."
end
if stroked_cat == true
"At the edge of the sign-up sheet, you absentmindedly draw a sleeping cat. It makes you smile."
end
if read_display == true
"You remember all those little purchases over the years. For a moment, the paper feels heavier."
end
if met_elena == true
show elena calm at left
end
if heard_elena == true
"Elena stops beside the noticeboard. She sees the pencil hovering in your hand and stands with you for a moment."
surface bubble
elena: "Don't write on Mateo's behalf. Listen to him first."
surface panel
end
"You write: 'Before deciding what to preserve, let's ask what the people who live and work here need.'"
if met_mateo == true
"Mateo reads it before anyone else. He doesn't smile, but the next day there's one more chair outside the shop."
else
"A note appears beneath yours: 'I hope they ask the owner first.' Signed with only an M."
end
if heard_rosa == true
"Rosa leaves a bag of paper cups. She says she'll bring coffee if someone else handles the chairs."
end
"By the next morning there are five replies. None agrees entirely with the others."
"The shutter rises just far enough to let the light in. Nobody promises the shop will stay open."
"But for one afternoon, at least, people stop speaking for each other."
"THE END — An invitation."

@scene ending_open
mode visual_novel
background street_evening
surface panel
if board_postponed == true
"The first time you saw the notice, you didn't know what to propose. Coming back doesn't make you an expert, but it makes you more careful with your plan."
end
if remembered_door == true
"You remember the wooden doorway and decide a proposal works better when it makes room for the person who must live with it."
end
if respected_privacy == true
"Before writing the plan, you cross out anything that would expose Mateo's private accounts."
end
"You write down volunteer shifts, a small raffle, and a community fund. You read the plan twice before posting it."
if mateo_wants_help == true
"Mateo appears with a blue pen. He asks where people can sign up to lend a hand."
else
"Mateo reads it in silence. You tell him the paper is only a proposal: he can say no."
end
if saw_ledger == true
"You remember the accounts you looked at without permission. You haven't mentioned them in the proposal, but that doesn't undo what you saw."
end
if heard_rosa == true
"Rosa adds that a meeting isn't a meeting if the people who shop there can't speak. You leave space for their names."
end
if heard_elena == true
"Elena corrects the meeting date and adds: 'No commitments until we've all talked.'"
end
"The shutter stays open that afternoon. Nobody knows for how long; nobody pretends to."
"A piece of paper can't save a neighborhood. Sometimes, though, it can get things started."
"THE END — A possibility."

@scene ending_quiet
mode visual_novel
background street_evening
surface panel
if board_postponed == true
"You came back to read the notice, and you still don't want to put your name under a decision that isn't yours. Returning doesn't oblige you to write."
end
if remembered_door == true
"The old doorway is still behind you. You've understood that remembering a place doesn't give you the right to decide its future."
end
if stroked_cat == true
"You remember the shop's cat. It didn't have to decide anyone's future to offer a moment of peace."
end
if saw_ledger == true
"The figures you saw in the shop won't leave your mind; they aren't yours to explain."
end
"You put the pencil back. You don't write an answer: you still don't know what yours would be."
if met_elena == true
"Elena doesn't ask what you decided. She walks beside you in silence for a while beneath the purple blossoms."
else
"Behind you, someone pins up the notice that had come loose."
end
if met_mateo == true
"You remember what Mateo said: closing can be a decision of his own. Your silence doesn't take that possibility away."
end
"The street is still beautiful, even as things change without asking permission."
"When you reach the corner, you see Mateo turn off a light. The one outside stays on."
"You haven't solved anything this afternoon. Tomorrow you can still come back."
"THE END — An open door."
